cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HERMES_Δ in your research, please cite the software as follows and the associated scientific paper listed in references."
title: "HERMES_Δ: High-Elective Resolution Modelling Emission System – Delta"
version: 1.0.11
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21393947
date-released: 2026-11-27
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: https://github.com/BSC-ES/HERMES_Delta
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21393947
abstract: >-
  HERMES_Δ (High-Elective Resolution Modelling Emission System – Delta) is an open-source,
  parallel emission processing and downscaling system designed to transform officially
  reported emission inventories into high-resolution, model-ready emission datasets for
  atmospheric chemistry and greenhouse gas simulations.

  The system processes emission inventories typically reported in aggregated tabular
  formats and applies a configurable workflow that performs chemical speciation, vertical
  distribution, temporal disaggregation and horizontal spatial allocation. Spatial
  allocation is performed using vector and raster activity proxies, while temporal profiles
  allow the transformation of annual emissions into hourly emissions. These transformations
  enable the generation of emission datasets suitable for direct use in atmospheric
  chemistry transport models.

  HERMES_Δ is implemented in Python and designed to run efficiently on high-performance
  computing (HPC) systems using MPI parallelization. All processing steps are controlled
  through configuration files (INI and YAML), allowing users to adapt the workflow to
  different emission inventories, spatial domains, sectors and modelling systems without
  modifying the source code.

  The system preserves traceability between the processed emissions and the original
  reported inventory data, facilitating transparent and reproducible emission modelling
  workflows. HERMES_Δ can therefore be used as the emission processing component of
  research or operational air-quality modelling systems.

  HERMES_Δ was developed as part of the high-Resolution air Emissions Systems to suPport
  modellIng and monitoRing Efforts (RESPIRE) national project (https://respire.bsc.es/).
  RESPIRE is part of Spain's Recovery, Transformation and Resilience Plan (Plan de
  Recuperación, Transformación y Resiliencia, PRTR), funded by the European Union –
  NextGenerationEU to support research and innovation initiatives following the COVID-19
  crisis.

  Source code: https://github.com/BSC-ES/HERMES_Delta

  Benchmark dataset:
  https://dataverse.bsc.es/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=perma:BSC/3ST00L

